## VERDICT
## **REJECT path-A close of 2.9** (walker → full `c_secret_emit_guard`)
SPRINT **2.9** (`println walker → full c_secret_emit_guard`) is **not**
a product land on this host or in the working tree.

1. Stmt `println` still special-cases in `c_emit_ident.oo` L129–131 →
   `c_emit_println` (`c_emit_print.oo` L9–85). Refuse is token IDENT +
   `c_secret_refuse_println_ident` (`__sec__` only). **Zero** calls to
   `c_secret_emit_guard` / `c_guard_scan_idents` in `c_emit_print.oo` or
   `c_emit_secret.oo`.
2. Check / LLVM front-door (`c_emit_secret.oo` L175–193) is still the
   inline IDENT walk + `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved`. SPRINT
   “What got fixed” **DE2.9** (`c_emit_secret.oo:175-186` →
   `c_secret_emit_guard(env, id, ...)`) is **false**. Those lines are
   the old walker. `c_secret_emit_guard` wants lowered C `a0/a1/a2/args`,
   not a token stream — the claimed call is a type mismatch.
3. Free-call lower (`c_emit_lower.oo` L90) **already** calls
   `c_secret_emit_guard`. Guard L223–225 lists `println` / `eprintln` /
   `print_err` / `log` / `fprintf` / `syslog`. Stmt `println` never
   reaches that rail. `eprintln` as a statement does (no ident special
   case). That split is the ticket. `s71_security.oot` R1 already named
   it **MED residual / unify later**.
4. Assigned **behavioral** red-team is **green dual-path** from a clean
   cwd. That proves the **old** token + check rails, not the helper.
   Official `s29_println_guard_smoke.oo` **exit 0** and itself prints:
   `RESIDUAL 2.9 walker→c_secret_emit_guard unify is Domain Expert
   product; this smoke proves refuse/no-FP`.
5. Regression: `secret_t1_return_smoke`, `secret_t2_depth_smoke`,
   `s28_macro_secret_smoke`, `s71_guard_scan_smoke` all **exit 0**.
   Official `s61_env_set_secretsink_smoke` **exit 1** on this stale
   host (check type-first). emit-c still `ERR\tsecret`. Same residual
   `s61_peer1.oot` already named. **Not a 2.9 FN.**

Do **not** over-claim: do **not** mark SPRINT 2.9 FIXED. Do **not**
treat DE2.9 as a close (`s29_hygiene.oot` agrees). Full IFC /
`#[Secret]` / `${}` stay residual. User-sink wrappers are **2.10**.

Assigned red-team is **not** a security FN. REJECT is **unify not
landed**, not a println SECRET hole.

